;; The DrThomasAger ontology. One tree, two roots, and the facets beside it.
;;
;; The tree says where a post lives. Every post has exactly one place, a
;; route from a root down to the most specific node that is wholly about it,
;; and its kicker is that route, e.g. "AI › Agents › AI Companions".
;; Each step down is a kind of, or a part of, the step above, at one
;; magnification finer, and the siblings at a step do not overlap.
;;
;; The facets say everything else about a post. They are tags from closed
;; vocabularies, many per post, used to filter, sort and search, by readers
;; and by MCPs reading index.json.
;;
;; Tiers, as the DrThomasAger lens magnifies:
;;   1 root     the half of the site, AI or Buddhism
;;   2 field    a field within it, e.g. Agents, Practice
;;   3 subject  a subject within the field, e.g. Multi-Agent Systems
;;   4 project  a named body of his own work with several posts, e.g. Ganapati
;;
;; Written 2026-10-08 under /C-auto from Hanjo's words, kept in README.md.
;; Changes are proposed with the reviewer and written by hand.

{:tiers [:root :field :subject :project]

 :tree
 [{:id :ai :label "AI" :also "Technology"
   :definition "Artificial intelligence as built and used, language models, prompts, agents and the systems made from them."
   :children
   [{:id :ai/language-models :label "Language Models"
     :definition "The models themselves, which model, at which size and quantization, and how it writes and behaves before any agent is built around it."
     :children
     [{:id :ai/local-models :label "Local Models"
       :definition "Running open models on one's own machine, engines, quants, windows and speed."}
      {:id :ai/model-behaviour :label "Model Behaviour"
